# Backend Engineering Standards

## Stack
.NET 10 + FastEndpoints + FastEndpoints.Swagger + MediatR + FluentValidation + EF Core + SQL Server + Serilog + xUnit/Moq

## Flow
Endpoint → Command/Query → Validator → Handler → Repository → EF Core

## Patterns
- Endpoint delegates to MediatR; no business logic
- Command/Query = record; Handler = IRequestHandler
- Validator required per Command/Query
- Repository interface in Application; impl in Infrastructure
- IEntityTypeConfiguration<T> for EF mappings

## Rules
- async/await + CancellationToken always
- record for DTOs/commands/queries
- Result<T> for outcomes, not exceptions
- Business logic in Application only
- Zero infrastructure refs in Application layer
- DB scripts (migrations, seeds, backups) live in /database, sibling of /src
